==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Chronos the Infinite''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Chronos''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Chronos is one of the best Uber Rares when it comes to freezing traited enemies effectively. Having a standing range of 450, she can hit many enemies in her large area of effect. She has 2-second gaps between her 3 multi-hits and 1-second gaps between her 3-second freezing. Chronos's use of multi-hit to deliver three short-duration Freeze procs instead of a single long Freeze is unique, and gives your meatshields more opportunities to gain and regain ground, which proves to be very effective throughout the game.

Her only real weakness as a crowd-controller is her lackluster up-time (10.3 seconds between attacks, 1-3 seconds of freeze depending on how many hit) as well as enemies that are either Immune to Freeze or resist it anyhow, such as Sages. However, since Freeze is the most powerful crowd control ability when it hits, she can compare favorably to the mighty [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]] on levels where the majority of enemies outrange your cats. Additionally, the large window her freezes create to attack enemies unopposed more than makes up for her inability to lock-down the field a majority of the time.

Chronos can be used to deal some damage to [[Henry]]; despite being unable to freeze him, she will be able to move into his blind spot without being frozen and freezing any other traited enemies in her range. Overall, she is a very versatile uber. Her freeze against traited enemies makes her a great generalist. With good meatshielding and three knockbacks, she will not get killed easily even in the frontlines.

It's recommended to summon her just before the main threat arrives, with your main attackers to ensure maximum damage. This way, she is at full HP when dealing with the boss. Her freezing will give your attackers time to deal massive damage.

==='''True Form'''===
Although True Forming her doesn't provide more of what she's good at, it gives her an immunity to Warp, which is useful in some situations and hurtful in others, but mostly good. The increase in stats isn't much to write home about, but given her huge value as a generalist, increasing both damage and health will always pay off. Shouldn't be a priority given her cost if you have other units you consider more important to evolve, but good, nonetheless.

==='''Talents'''===
None of the Resist Talents are worth considering. However, Resist Curse might be useful when you meet enemies like [[Loris]] and can't avoid getting hit, but it's pretty situational and shouldn't be invested in unless you decide to put a curse resist A-grade orb on her so she becomes completely Immune to Curse.

Move Speed Up is mostly detrimental, since a unit with [[Long Distance]] doesn't go well with high speed, which can make her move forward when enemies are knocked back and accidentally put them inside her blindspot.

Defense Buff and Attack Buff are the standard for most [[Talents|Talented]] units, but less relevant for Chronos. Defense should take priority over attack, and [[Catseye]]s should take priority over Talents.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''[[Surge Attack]]''' is extremely powerful, with the lingering hitboxes both creating a wall of Freeze that paralyzes enemies not hit by the initial attack, as well as extending each Freeze to 1.7-seconds against Fruited traits (1.5-seconds normally), giving Chronos the potential to almost fully lock down targets without a "stuttering" effect, on top of raising her DPS by a whopping 50%. This is easily her best Talent, and the reason to get Chronos to Lv.60.

'''[[Immune to Surge]]''' gives her viability against piercing Surge attackers that would normally shut her down. Enemies like [[St. Dober]], [[Medu-san]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]], [[Omens]], and even the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] are all good matchups now. Furthermore, Counter-Surgers that would normally feed off of her constant Surge spam won't pose any issue to her either. This does not protect any other meatshields or attackers you bring alongside her, however, so do beware of the problems that can cause.

While Chronos is not primarily used for damage, '''[[Colossus Slayer]]''' makes her a slightly stronger option in [[Gauntlet|Colossus Gauntlets]], turning her into a better attacker with up to ~20,500 DPS vs Colossus enemies. These stages are littered with hyper-aggressive, high magnification enemies that usually rely on their raw numbers to push, making Chronos's Freeze, especially when improved with Surges, perfect for holding them still for your other attackers. But the benefits on this Talent only show with the boss itself, and defensive bonus doesn't do much, given how much damage these bosses do, to the point where anything in their line of sight may as well be considered dead. Furthermore, she's still highly susceptible to pierce, and struggles greatly with the [[Tackey]] in [[Horrorpotamus/Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.1~20|Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.11~20]], [[Gigahaniwan]]'s Wave Attacks, [[Big Peng Z]]'s Omni Strikes, and the Mini-Wave spam in [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Blessing Lv.1~20|Blessing Lv.11~20]]. She generally does well in most other Gauntlets, though, but that's true with or without this Talent. Don't bother getting it if you must be frugal with NP.

==='''Orb'''===
As mentioned before, the only Orb worth considering on Chronos is a Grade A Curse Resist Orb to protect her from said ability with help from her Curse Resist Talent.

